        "text": "<!DOCTYPE html><html><head></head><body><p>In Thermodynamics we studied about spontaneity of a reaction based on Gibb's free energy values which is an energytic perspective but how much time that reaction will complete is also an important perspective for the spontaneity of a reaction. In this chapter, we deal with that time perspective of a reaction. Here we got knowledge about the rate and time of completion of a reaction and it has vast applications in various processes like carbon dating, nuclear reactions kinetics, etc. A very good amount of questions arise from this chapter in various examinations.</p></body></html>",
